  "notes": "All 283 town/House-district/Senate-district reporting splits match the election metadata and reconcile every candidate, named write-in, blank and overvote to the statewide House rollup. The compact display's other column includes blanks/overvotes and is not used as candidate votes. These are not established polling precincts; no map or precinct turnout is published. Separate 247-town registration/ballot counts retain five House-accounting discrepancies and Colchester's different district count; all six affected municipal rates are withheld, not repaired. Remaining rates are provisional municipal registered-voter fractions, not citizen/resident turnout or demographic estimates. All nine complete original JSON feeds are retained, including all six enabled office tabs and turnout. Only the federal House counts and municipal turnout are normalized; other offices remain unreviewed. The generic SOS information page returned 403; the normal public results portal was accessible.",
  "next_action": "Acquire official 2026 town/legislative-split or polling geography with an explicit identity crosswalk; do not map split counts onto whole towns. Resolve Colchester's district scope, five municipal ballot discrepancies and registration definitions; reconcile the remaining preserved office tabs."
